{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"uneasy-skilled-seagull","creation_channel":"cli","description":"## Problem\n\nThe `rebar-implement` skill (examples/agent-skills/rebar-implement/SKILL.md) carries a \"Model\ntiering\" section that pins the implementer subagent to strong/standard/cheap model tiers to\nsave tokens. This model-level gradient adds significant complexity (a tier table, per-dispatch\ntier-naming rules, a dedicated 4e-bis \"Tier escalation\" ladder, and per-leaf tiering session-log\nrequirements) for savings that only materialize on wide epics. We are removing it.\n\nSeparately, Phase 0's preflight hard-stops on any ticket with no children, telling the user to\ndecompose first. That is too strict: a `story`/`task` that has no children but DOES carry a\nrecorded file impact is already an executable code leaf — the file impact is exactly the\nacceptance the completion-verifier close gate needs. The skill should execute such a ticket as a\nsingle leaf instead of refusing it.\n\n## Plan\n\n1. Remove the model-level gradient:\n   - Delete the entire \"## Model tiering\" section.\n   - Strip tiering language from every downstream reference (Phase 3 non-code leaf, 4a spec\n     derivation, 4d implementer dispatch + constraints note) while PRESERVING the held-out\n     discipline (the implementer remains a *separate subagent*, which never depended on tiering).\n   - Rewrite 4e-bis from \"Tier escalation\" to a tier-free \"Escalation — when re-dispatch isn't\n     enough\" (re-dispatch -> take-the-leaf-yourself -> report blocked).\n   - Reground the Phase 5 residual-sweep example that referenced tier-based validation.\n\n2. Allow a childless story/task with a recorded file impact to run as a single leaf:\n   - Phase 0 now recognizes two executable shapes: (a) has children -> tree; (b) childless\n     `story`/`task` with non-empty `rebar get-file-impact` -> single code leaf. Stop only when\n     neither holds.\n   - Add a Phase 2 callout so the epic ceremony (Phases 3/5/6) collapses to one change for the\n     single-leaf run.\n   - Update the frontmatter description, the Phase 0 heading, and the Reporting stop line to\n     match.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- No \"Model tiering\" section and no model strong/standard/cheap tier references remain in\n  SKILL.md (the surviving \"tier\" wording refers only to *test* tiers from test-design.md).\n- The held-out separation (separate implementer subagent) is preserved everywhere.\n- Phase 0 executes a childless `story`/`task` with a non-empty file impact as a single code\n  leaf, and still stops cleanly for a childless ticket with no file impact.\n- Frontmatter description, Phase 0 heading, Phase 2, and Reporting are all consistent with the\n  two changes.\n- Docs-only change; no code, so `make lint`/`typecheck`/`test` are unaffected.","id":"2b4f-b0ca-e5d8-4c3f","parent_id":"","priority":2,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"task","title":"rebar-implement: remove model-tiering gradient; run a childless story/task with file impact as a single leaf"},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1786140869666001001,"uuid":"11fd934d-80ad-422d-aba2-2e08de76630a"}